# Scrolling with the wheel. Needs -debug-events and *no* TEXMACS_VUE_SNAPSHOT:
# the checks are on the deltas in SI of the "handling wheel" lines of the log,
# and saving a PNG per frame would stretch the iterations of the loop past the
# 16 ms which tell a second notch from a swipe (see wheel_event in vue_gui.cpp).
# The cursor is at the end, so the wheel scrolls up.
#
#  * a notch is not a jump: the first stream below asks for 3 x 80 points
#    (3 x 80 x 256 = 61440 SI) and travels them over some twenty frames with
#    decaying deltas
#  * three more notches 40 ms apart add up: the deltas rise again at each of
#    them and the view comes to rest shortly after the last one, having
#    travelled 3 x 61440 SI in all
#  * a swipe which opens with a whole delta must scroll the ten points of a
#    unit and not the eighty of a notch: the deltas of the last stream add up
#    to (1 + 0.4 + 0.5 + 0.3) x 10 x 256 = 5632 SI and none of them is
#    negative, nothing having to be taken back
wait 7000
window #2
# the document is inserted by wheel-travel.scm
wait 500
wheel 300 400 0 3
wait 700
wheel 300 400 0 3
wait 40
wheel 300 400 0 3
wait 40
wheel 300 400 0 3
wait 900
wheel 300 400 0 1
wait 10
wheel 300 400 0 0.4
wait 10
wheel 300 400 0 0.5
wait 10
wheel 300 400 0 0.3
wait 900
